| **i116** | **Harness measurement / byte-match tests must assert the build succeeded — no stale-`.bin` reads** (i104 retro pattern, 4 sessions: `sha256-fastest-z80`, `i88-tls-go-authority-arc`, `i48c-expr-parser-bricks`, + a timestamp-keyed no-op variant). A failed `pyz80`/`make` build leaves the *previous* `.bin` in place (or a timestamp-keyed target no-ops after a source restore), so a T-state or byte-identical check reads the **stale** artifact and reports ✅ — masking the failure (one "byte-identical IDENTICAL" actually compared against a build that had errored). The i21 `USAGE.md` doc note **did not take** ("it's documented… but it bit again"), so the fix is **structural, not another doc line**: make the harness measurement / oracle tests **depend on the `.bin` build target** (or assert build exit-0 / a freshness check) so they cannot run against a stale artifact. Agent-ownable harness evolution (the "agents own the harness" rule). | OPEN — 🔨 small harness change; autonomous-eligible | `tools/z80-test-harness-go/`; the i21 `USAGE.md` doc note that did not take; `~/claude-retro/` (i104 source); i104, i21 |
| **i117** | **Extract the sam-aarch64 learnings into a reusable, open-source "autonomous Claude project" framework** (Pete, 2026-06-18 — a future deliverable, **open-source for any Claude user**, possibly shipped as a **Claude Code plugin**). A starter framework/template so a *new* project inherits the properties that made this one work without re-deriving them: the **autonomous-loop monitor** (i97 — the deterministic `screen`-driven `/context`→nudge→`/clear` loop), the **split `iN`/`qN` registries** + controlled-status discipline (+ the i115 validator once built), the **§3 pre-merge review gate** + merge-authority-stays-with-orchestrator rule, the **per-session retro practice** (i104) + its aggregation loop, the **prime-directive verification** ethos, the **brick + Go-authority-oracle + mutation-teeth** loop, **delegate-to-subagents** context discipline, and the **doc-lifecycle + single-source-of-truth** rules. **Load-bearing requirement (Pete):** it must carry the portable, project-agnostic principles that today live in Pete's *non-repo* global `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (which other users won't have), so the framework is **self-contained and usable by anyone**, not dependent on Pete's personal config. **Delivery options:** a template repo / `init` scaffold (parameterised `CLAUDE.md` + `tools/autonomous-loop/` + registry skeletons + retro/diary scaffolding + a setup README), and/or a **Claude Code plugin** bundling the hooks + skills + the monitor + the doc skeletons. Open-sourcing it benefits the whole Claude community, not just this project. | BLOCKED:Pete — future open-source meta-deliverable; scope + sequencing + packaging (template repo vs Claude plugin) are Pete's call; do not auto-pick-up | this whole repo as the source corpus; `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (global principles to port out); i97 (monitor), i104 (retro), i115 (registry validator); ROADMAP handover contract |
